// Syncthing's own ignore file — separate from .gitignore. Rewritten 2026-08-15
// after a real sync conflict: the first version only excluded .git itself,
// which left Syncthing ALSO managing every git-tracked working-tree file
// (scripts/, CLAUDE.md, README.md, etc.) alongside git's own push/pull — two
// systems both trying to own the same files, and a genuine conflict
// (.sync-conflict-*.gitignore) showed up almost immediately from the two
// machines' git clones having different line-ending normalization.
//
// Correct division of ownership: git owns everything it tracks (push/pull is
// the sync mechanism there — see NEW-MACHINE-SETUP.md). Syncthing owns only
// what git deliberately excludes (see .gitignore) — the real vault content.
// This list is the inverse of .gitignore's content list: only these paths
// are synced, everything else is ignored by Syncthing (owned by git instead).
!Sources
!Concepts
!Protocols
!Daily
!Synthesis
!Research
!Logs
!Bases
!People
!Dashboard
!Bloodwork
!Optimization
!YouTube Queue.md
!Podcast Queue.md
!wiki
!index.md
!log.md
!development.md
!buglog.md
!ideas.md
!.env
!.env.*
!*.token
!*credentials*.json
!*.docx
!*.canvas
!tmp_transcripts
*
